<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Reef/square-knot glyph, real geometry transcribed from Wikimedia Commons'
     public-domain "Square knot.svg" diagram (not hand-drawn), recolored and
     fit to our badge. Path order matters: it's what makes the grey strand's
     tail ends cross over the white loop on the left while its own belly curve
     stays tucked under it, the way a real square knot's strands alternate.

     The whole badge (silver ring + green + knot) is drawn self-contained in
     this foreground layer, scaled to fit inside a 66dp-diameter circle (r=33
     of the 108dp viewport) - Android's guaranteed-always-visible adaptive-icon
     safe zone. The first version relied on the background color showing
     through as a ring around a full-size (r=46) green circle, but most
     launchers mask well inside that, so the ring never actually showed on a
     real device. -->
